    "narrative": "For the June 14 slate, the Austin Waves offense centers on three primary anchors who boast the most favorable conditions for production. **Jackson Merrill** (72.01) and **Kyle Tucker** (71.48) are our top outfield plays, benefiting significantly from favorable park factors and the \"Wind Out\" condition. **Gunnar Henderson** remains the day's highest-upscale engine (81.88) against Buehler; his elite efficiency is fueled by a 16% park boost and the rare confluence of a favorable matchup and high-order placement. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (70.52) similarly benefits from the lineup order and platoon dynamics against Hancock, making the middle-infield duo of **Gunnar Henderson** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** the primary catalyst for our Roto output today.\n\nWhile we are leaning into high-upside starters, the selection process required tough calls at the margins. **Wade Meckler** (45.25) was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine; despite a decent projection and an attractive hitting environment against Legumina, his efficiency profile lagged slightly behind the defensive and speed-adjusted metrics of **Nasim Nunez** and **Sam Antonacci**. We are keeping **Wade Meckler** in reserve to maintain strict adherence to our game cap strategy. We must also exercise caution with **Liam Hicks** (41.15), whose score is suppressed by a difficult assignment against Skenes. His inclusion is a strategic necessity, but his low efficiency score relative to his base projection serves as a warning that he is our primary \"floor\" play today, rather than a primary source of categorical gain.",
